# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A managed workflow job works like a batch job that you submit to an HPC scheduler. `run()` submits the job and returns a `Job` object immediately. Use the `Job` object for the tasks that `squeue`, the job's output file, and `scancel` cover on a cluster. The job keeps running after you close your notebook.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Job aliran kerja terurus berfungsi seperti job kelompok yang anda hantar kepada penjadual HPC. `run()` menghantar job dan segera mengembalikan objek `Job`. Gunakan objek `Job` untuk tugas yang dilakukan oleh `squeue`, fail output job dan `scancel` pada kluster. Job terus berjalan selepas anda menutup buku nota anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The examples on this page use a small workflow that reads one angle, `theta`, and fails if the angle is out of range. Upload it as described in [Deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Contoh pada halaman ini menggunakan aliran kerja kecil yang membaca satu sudut, `theta`, dan gagal jika sudut berada di luar julat. Muat naiknya seperti yang diterangkan dalam [Gunakan aliran kerja terurus pertama anda](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"

